    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. Here's what I changed to consolidate duplicate detection into a single `identityKey`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The one key** \u2014 new `OwnerIdentity.key(owner)` (`rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java`) derives:\n```\nnormalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)\n```\nusing the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` (E.164) and lower-cased/trimmed email, exactly as the spec dictates.\n\n**Single duplicate check** \u2014 new `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` scans existing owners and throws a new 409 `DuplicateIdentityException` **only when the whole `identityKey` matches**. This replaces the three separate checks:\n- Deleted `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, `CheckOwnerEmailUnique`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` and their `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes, handlers, and escalation YAMLs.\n- Added `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateIdentityException.yml` (409 CONFLICT, same `ProblemDetail` shape).\n\n**Household id still assigned, just no longer a reject** \u2014 the household-matching/stamping logic was preserved in a repurposed `AssignOwnerHousehold` step (same `sharesHousehold` opt-in, same stable `H-\u2026` id stamped on all members) but with the rejection removed. Because `householdId` is part of the key, two household members with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed \u2014 the explicit behaviour change.\n\n**Pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`): `build \u2192 assignHousehold \u2192 checkIdentity \u2192 checkCityCapacity \u2192 \u2026`, so the key is computed only after the telephone/email/householdId are final.\n\n**Returning it** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (regenerated into `OwnerDto`) and mapped it in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` via `OwnerIdentity.key(owner)`, so every owner response includes it.\n\nTest result:\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n`coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (two owners sharing a telephone, both with empty email/householdId \u2192 identical `identityKey`) now returns 409 through the single consolidated check.",
